A||N||4||dgroves||Tranny selector cable||||5||
Z||000000||dgroves||06-08-2001||01:55 PM||||Purchased car ('86 GT Fastback W/2.8 Liter & auto) after botched engine swap. Some parts were not replaced. One of these was the bracket that attaches the shift cable to the tranny. I found a bracket in a junk yard but it lacks about an inch of being long enough to work. Are there variations from year to year in the cables/brackets? Easiest solution would be to add needed length to bracket .... yes/no?<P>Yes, the adjuster is collapsed all the way to the stop.||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||06-08-2001||04:37 PM||||The Fiero trans to cable bracket and lever are unique to the Fiero. You need a Fiero bracket and lever.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT-maniac||06-09-2001||12:54 AM||||TerryK is right you should look for the proper bracket froma fiero. I'd try the used fiero part vendors first as bracket for anything on the fiero are incredibly expensive. I had to replace a clutch bracket on my 4 spd and it cost me over 100 bucks from the dealers. I've had good experience with FieroDave or the fiero warehouse or you try some of the others. Just click on the vendors button at the top of the forum page.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||06-09-2001||07:21 AM||||The V6 and 4 cyl Fieros use different brackets. How do I know? I did a 4 speed auto swap in an '87 GT, I fabricated the shift cable brackets using an old 4cyl cable and shifter I had. When I got the setup back into the car, the V6 cable didn't fit, it was either too long or too short, I don't remember. I installed the 4cyl cable into the car and everything fits fine. The V6 cable has an adjustment on the end, the 4cyl cable doesn't.||||reg||1
Z||000004||dgroves||06-09-2001||11:08 AM||||The bracket I have is from a V-6 auto. It's too short. Thats why I asked if there are variations per model year. I noticed that the donor car had a different dust cover than the cable on my car. The adjustor seemed to be the same and it fits perfectly except the cable end sticks about an inch and a quarter past the slot in the shifter arm on the tranny. <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>The Fiero trans to cable bracket and lever are unique to the Fiero. You need a Fiero bracket and lever.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
